# A list and a view of any kind are read in one turn. Turns were laid out either once for each kind of a view or once for each storage of a list, and where both stood in a turn, not at all: nine kinds by two
# storages. So the table was read by the chain of kinds in every turn: a thousand elements 39,124 instructions, plain Bun 13,592. The turns are laid out by the view's kind alone; whether the list holds doubles or
# int32s is read once in front as a value, and each read branches on it. 20,154.
# RUN: compile LoopsLaidOutForEachKindOfView KindsOfListsReadInFrontOfTurnsLaidOut mechanisms=all
# CHECK: statistic LoopsLaidOutForEachKindOfView 4
# CHECK-NOT: statistic KindsOfListsReadInFrontOfTurnsLaidOut 0
